  "title": "Compost Commons",
  "rules": [
    "One gardener can tow the real compost cart. A worker can instead carry a screen, a compost portion or one produce batch; water uses a separate flask.",
    "The finite pile matures at moisture two through four. Turning adds two progress and emits odor; mature quality begins at six.",
    "Adding raw material at the sorting station resets the entire pile's age. Scooped portions retain their immature or mature quality while carried.",
    "Immature compost adds two crop growth and two stress. Mature compost adds three growth and one moisture. Scoop tools must be cleaned before another scoop.",
    "An active odor point attracts pests. Wind moves the point on even ticks and sets pest tie order; deployed screens repel entry and protect crops within one cell.",
    "Pests move actual cardinal cells and respect irrigation channels and bridges. Crop contact removes water and adds stress; stress four kills.",
    "Harvest a ripe patch once for two produce. Store privately at your stall or donate at the common barn; only donated produce counts toward six.",
    "Everything shown is native state. Human/policy actions are identical and all author scripts remain unexecuted."
  ],
